From feeed790c69c6e0b0a4130e683350d52cea180a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kwuang Tang <arctangent20@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:26:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] three r187 (latest): PMREM cube-target env blend, CSM breaks,
 vColor vec4, Timer, HDRLoader, PCFShadowMap

- three ^0.170 -> ^0.187.0, @types/three ^0.187.0
- lighting.ts: CubeUVReflectionMapping was removed (r187 PMREMs are cube render targets with
  explicit mip levels): the blended sky environment is now a PMREM-shaped WebGLCubeRenderTarget
  (isPMREMTexture, 256 px, mips to 8 px) rendered per mip level and face from the source PMREMs
  with a samplerCube/textureLod blend material and a CubeCamera
- lighting.ts: CSM.getExtendedBreaks() is private now: the [prev, break] pairs are rebuilt from
  the public csm.breaks; dropped the getPointShadow patch of CSMShader (fixed upstream)
- lighting.ts: RGBELoader (deprecated r180) -> HDRLoader
- main.ts: PCFSoftShadowMap (deprecated r182) -> PCFShadowMap; THREE.Clock (deprecated r183) -> THREE.Timer
- buildings-shop.ts, shopkit/filler.ts: vColor is always vec4 in the shaders now (use .rgb)
- tests/crossing.test.ts: Box3.setFromObject no longer recomputes stale world matrices (r185),
  so frozen pedestrians are posed before their stature is measured
- type fixes: materials.ts (defines), district-showcase.ts (morphAttributes)

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean; npm run build ok; npm run qa 260/260 (interior 14/14); headless
Chromium: world, museum and ~20 labs compile every program (no shader errors) and render.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BpmvtRPd6KcQVro9zRPwoL
